  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Procure > Finalise and publish procurement pack",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This regulation provides rules on how a contracting authority must publish the procurement documents. The contracting authority must offer unrestricted and full direct access free of charge to the procurement documents, by means of the internet, from the date of the publication of the procurement notices on the UK e-notification service (provided by Find a Tender). The content of the notice must specify the internet address at which the procurement documents are accessible.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Where, in accordance with the exemptions under regulation 22(3) PCR 2015 (rules applicable to communication), the contracting authority does not offer access via the internet to the procurement documents, the contracting authority may indicate in the notice that the procurement documents concerned will be transmitted by other means.",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Additionally, where the contracting authority intends to impose requirements aimed at protecting the confidential nature of the relevant information (as per regulation 21 PCR 2015 (Confidentiality)), it must indicate in the notice which measures are required and how access can be obtained.",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In both of the situations above, the time limit for the submission of tenders must be extended by five days (except in the cases of duly substantiated urgency).",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "If requested in good time, contracting authorities must provide to all tenderers any additional information relating to the specifications and / or any supporting documents, no later than six days before the deadline for the receipt of tenders. This may be reduced to four days in the case of an accelerated procedure.",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The contract notice must indicate where the procurement documents can be accessed by interested suppliers.",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Contracting authorities should:",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "offer unrestricted and full direct access free of charge to the procurement documents, by means of the internet, from the date of the publication of the following notices on Find a Tender: contract notice under regulation 49 PCR 2015 and design contest notice under regulation 79 PCR 2015",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "specify in the notice the internet address at which the procurement documents are accessible",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "where unrestricted and full direct access free of charge to certain procurement documents cannot be offered via the internet for one of the reasons set out in regulation 22(3) PCR 2015 (rules applicable to communication), indicate in the notice that the procurement documents will be transmitted by other means",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "where unrestricted and full direct access free of charge to certain procurement documents cannot be offered via the internet for reasons set out in regulation 21(3) PCR 2015 (confidentiality), indicate in the notice which measures are required for the protection of confidential information and how access to the procurement documents can be obtained.",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "Electronic availability of procurement documents",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00016",
